  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1059 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\n00Z upper air analysis shows an upper-level ridge encompassing\nmuch of the Central/Southern Plains and Middle/Lower Mississippi\nValleys this evening. Meanwhile, surface high pressure remains \ncentered over the Mid-Atlantic states. This is resulting in a \ncontinuation of dry conditions across the Mid-South with well \nabove normal temperatures for late August. Late evening \ntemperatures are predominantly in the 70s across the area.\n\nThe aforementioned surface high will push east on Sunday allowing\nsoutherly winds on the back side of high pressure to develop and\nadvect higher dewpoint air back into the area, especially east of\nthe Mississippi River. Temperatures on Sunday will rise into the\nmiddle to upper 90s as the upper-level ridge strengthens across\nthe Lower Mississippi Valley.\n\nThis ridge will result in a mainly dry and very hot persistence\nforecast across the Mid-South for most of next week. A\ncombination of daily highs in the upper 90s to around 100 degrees\nwith the gradually rising humidity will result in heat index\nvalues approaching or exceeding 105 degrees in some locations\nperhaps as early as Monday across portions of northwest\nMississippi and East Arkansas (south of I-40). Confidence is \nhigher for heat headlines occurring mid to late week. A weak \ntropical wave in the northern Gulf may bring a slight chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms towards next weekend to portions of \nnorth Mississippi.",
